mcp_tool_registry — retained server obligations
==================================================

Status: retained contract; current carve-out verification pending.

Keep MCP_Registry and MCP_Tool registration, duplicate rejection, import merge, activation, builtin-form advertising and tool output capture. Registries remain Isabelle context data. Imports merge ancestor declarations into descendants; declarations do not update ancestors.

The startup root is always a private temporary live PIDE wrapper importing exactly the selected -T theory, whether image or source. Its context supplies the catalogue and default execution on each list and call. Resolve the current root theory again, so reprocessing an ancestor and then the wrapper updates subsequent calls. A per-call target chooses only execution context. Select the actual tool value from the root, then invoke that value in the ML-resolved target; do not look up its name again in the target. Default calls execute at the root. Preserve imported/sibling isolation tests and declaration-triggered tools/list_changed notifications.

Every ML tool automatically advertises optional String context in ordinary
arguments. The framework resolves that target URL in ML and strips context
before calling the root-selected tool's unchanged #run. Absence defaults to the
root. Reject declaration of a tool-owned context parameter clearly; authors do
not resolve targets themselves. Scala builtins do not gain context.

Verification obligations
------------------------

T1 [ml-unit] HOL-safe MCP registration permits ordinary datatype declarations and simplifier proofs with MCP both before and after another HOL theory in the imports. Both import-order fixtures exercise registration and retain their own exported test metadata.

T2 [ml-unit] Capture-form tools return printed output, join output with failures, expose all validated declared arguments including defaults, reject undeclared argument lookup, and preserve interrupt/output isolation between invocations.
